### Strip non-whitelisted properties with whitelist option

Source: https://github.com/nestjs/docs.nestjs.com/blob/master/content/application/validation.md

Enable the whitelist: true option to automatically strip any properties from the incoming request payload that do not have validation decorators in the DTO. You can additionally set forbidNonWhitelisted: true to reject requests containing unknown properties.

```typescript
app.useGlobalPipes(
  new ValidationPipe({
    whitelist: true,
  }),
);
```

--------------------------------

### Enable payload auto-transformation globally

Source: https://github.com/nestjs/docs.nestjs.com/blob/master/content/application/validation.md

Configure ValidationPipe globally with transform: true to automatically instantiate DTO classes and convert primitive parameter types across all endpoints.

```typescript
app.useGlobalPipes(
  new ValidationPipe({
    transform: true,
  }),
);
```

--------------------------------

### Stripping properties

Source: https://github.com/nestjs/docs.nestjs.com/blob/master/content/application/validation.md

`ValidationPipe` can also filter out properties that the route handler should not receive. When you **whitelist** the acceptable properties, any property not included in the whitelist is stripped from the resulting object. For example, if the handler expects `email` and `password`, but a request also includes an `age` property, `age` is removed from the resulting DTO. To enable this behavior, set `whitelist` to `true`.

With this option enabled, properties without any decorator in the validation class are removed.

Alternatively, you can reject requests that contain non-whitelisted properties with an error response. To do so, set `forbidNonWhitelisted` to `true` in addition to `whitelist`.

--------------------------------

### Expose DTO properties with @ApiProperty decorator

Source: https://github.com/nestjs/docs.nestjs.com/blob/master/content/openapi/types-and-parameters.md

Annotates class properties so they are visible to SwaggerModule when generating model definitions. Alternatively, the Swagger CLI plugin can generate these annotations automatically.

```typescript
import { ApiProperty } from '@nestjs/swagger';

export class CreateCatDto {
  @ApiProperty()
  name: string;

  @ApiProperty()
  age: number;

  @ApiProperty()
  breed: string;
}
```

--------------------------------

### Convert primitive route parameters with transform enabled

Source: https://github.com/nestjs/docs.nestjs.com/blob/master/content/application/validation.md

When transform: true is active on ValidationPipe, primitive path and query parameters are automatically converted from strings to their declared TypeScript types such as number.

```typescript
@Get(':id')
findOne(@Param('id') id: number) {
  console.log(typeof id === 'number'); // true
  return 'This action returns a user';
}
```
